## vm.args for the swarm release (a Mix release picks rel/vm.args.eex up
## automatically). Fixes the inet_dist port to a single, known value so
## k8s/deployment.yaml can declare a fixed containerPort (9000) and the
## NetworkPolicy can allow exactly that port.
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 9000
-kernel inet_dist_listen_max 9000

## Distribution transport: TLS, not cleartext (DEP-07 / SEC-10). The
## `-proto_dist inet_tls -ssl_dist_optfile ...` flags are injected by
## rel/env.sh.eex through ELIXIR_ERL_OPTIONS, not written here, because the
## optfile path is relative to the release root ($RELEASE_ROOT/ssl_dist.conf)
## and vm.args has no variable expansion. Putting them in env.sh also makes
## them apply to `bin/swarm_node rpc` / `remote`, whose hidden node must speak
## the same TLS distribution to reach this node.
##
## Memory / scheduling: the Erlang VM is cgroup-aware for CPU quota (OTP 23+),
## so schedulers-online follow the pod's CPU limit. SWARM_SCHEDULERS in
## rel/env.sh.eex pins +S explicitly when the operator wants it.
## Bound the number of ports/sockets (default 65536 on most OSes -> explicit).
+Q 65536

## RELEASE_NODE/RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION/RELEASE_COOKIE (set via k8s env, with
## RELEASE_NODE=swarm_node@$(POD_IP)) configure -name/-setcookie through the
## release's own boot script.
